       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 4 g/day, and some institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the normal maximum of 1000 mg. At 15 g/day, this could cause serious liver injury even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you meant something different, check with your supervising resident or pharmacist."
