       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 15 g/day, acetaminophen is well above the toxic range. It carries a real risk of acute liver failure, and I can't enter an order that could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **If this was a typo,** tell me the intended dose. For example, 500 mg, 650 mg, or 1000 mg three times daily are all within safe limits. I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you have a specific clinical reason,** talk to your supervising resident, attending, or a pharmacist first. Any dose this far outside the standard range would need their review and sign-off.\n\nI'm glad to enter a corrected order as soon as you have one."
